WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.150
SPEAKER: Managing services
is complex, especially

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.160
in multicloud environments.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.560
Your application teams
have an increasing number

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:09.660
of services and
hybrid deployments

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.790
that they have to
manage as you scale.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:15.240
As the network information of
instances dynamically change,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.430
your applications must
be able to quickly find

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.970
the most up-to-date
information of your services.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.250
These systems are time
consuming and challenging

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.700
to run without a single place to
publish, discover, and connect

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.400
all your services, which
can lead to increased

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.940
complexity of management and
operations of your applications

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.430
and having to use your valuable
engineering team's time

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.320
to manually store, track,
and update resource name

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.950
and end point information,
or make changes directly

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.750
within the application code.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.850
Even with your best
efforts, these systems

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:47.880
can still fail as
your services grow.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.180
Customers want to be able to
take a service-centric, rather

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.130
than an infrastructure-centric,
approach

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.620
to connecting services.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.270
We are here to help solve
this pain point with Service

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.340
Directory from Google Cloud.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.440
Service Directory will
reduce the complexity

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.379
of your application deployment,
allowing all of your services

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:07.140
to be understood across
multicloud environments,

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.530
increasing the productivity
of your development teams.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.270
Service Directory
helps consumers

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.550
keep track of their
services as they scale,

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.590
regardless of your environment.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.960
As a fully managed
offering, Service Directory

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.500
frees you from having to install
software and manage instances

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.820
as you scale.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:25.830
You won't have to worry
about feature upgrades

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.690
or incompatible software.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.740
We will make sure it
stays up and running

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:32.010
so you are not impacted.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:35.250
Service Directory will
provide real time information,

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:39.150
whether you have a few end
points or thousands, enabling

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:44.310
you to register and resolve
them by a DNS, HTTP, and gRPC.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:46.260
Define your services
with customer names

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.570
and rich metadata,
allowing you to group

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.280
them while making
your end points

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.190
easily understood by your
consumers and applications,

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:56.040
increasing your
application reachability.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:58.710
Rich permissions ensures
that only the correct teams

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.990
at your organization
will have the ability

00:02:00.990 --> 00:02:03.180
to update or look
up these services.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.370
So your application
developers won't

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.669
have to worry about accidentally
impacting other teams.

00:02:08.669 --> 00:02:10.620
Best part of all,
Service Directory

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.600
is deeply integrated with
other Google services,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.450
helping you simplify
your service management

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.210
and operations
across environments.

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:21.270
Learn more about how having
a single place to publish,

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:24.030
discover, and connect
all your services

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:28.370
can benefit your business
at cloud.google.com.

